<h2>This website aims to:</h2>
<hr />
<h3>Showcase our Kingdom</h3>
<p>
  This website acts as the hub for all information related to the Plushie Kingdom, including how to
  get started living here, what life here is like, and where to get any needed help.
</p>
<h3>Strengthen the Government's identity</h3>
<p>
  pk-gov is more than just a website, it's the core of our
  <a class='link' href='/dev/design/gov-identity/'>identity</a>
  : Bold and modern, yet warm and welcoming. We ensure plushies are confident that the information
  or services they're viewing is of high quality and relevant to them whenever they see the familiar
  colours, iconography and font, no matter where it may be.
</p>
<h3>Provide Government information and services</h3>
<p>
  In our efforts to create a digital-first Government, all Government information and services will
  be made available here, ensuring plushies can access them anywhere, anytime.
</p>
<h3>Keep citizens informed</h3>
<p>
  The
  <a class='link' href='/news/'>Government news page</a>
  will be home to news updates on various topics relevant to the Plushie Kingdom, such as new
  services, travel alerts or other important information. Video versions may also be available for
  major announcements on our
  <a
    class='link'
    href='https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCL4Px1LLyD6WxcaDTm71ViQ'
    target='_blank'
    rel='noreferrer'
  >YouTube channel</a>.
</p>
<h2>History of pk-gov</h2>
<hr />
<h3>Early beginnings - May 2026</h3>
<p>
  After the formation of the Plushie Kingdom Government, Prime Minister Pink Bear Bear and
  Technology Minister Android envisioned a digital-first future, where plushies could freely access
  Government information and services through a centralised website. On 2 May 2026, the
  <a class='link' href='https://github.com/J0e-Quan/pk-gov' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>
    pk-gov repository
  </a>
  was created to make this future possible. The creation of the
  <a
    class='link'
    href='https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCL4Px1LLyD6WxcaDTm71ViQ'
    target='_blank'
    rel='noreferrer'
  >Plushie Kingdom Government YouTube channel</a>
  soon followed, to provide a platform for video announcements.
</p>
<h3>Implementation of Government news - May 2026</h3>
<p>
  On 8 May 2026, Government news was integrated into the pk-gov website, allowing for rapid delivery
  of information from the Government to Plushie Kingdom citizens. The first use of this would be an
  <a class='link' href='/news/introducing-the-plushie-kingdom-government'>
    introduction to the Plushie Kingdom Government
  </a>
  , delivered by the Prime Minister.
</p>
<h3>Introduction of responsive design - May 2026</h3>
<p>
  The pk-gov website implemented responsive design on 13 May 2026, ensuring that the website
  remained intuitive and easy to use on mobile devices.
</p>
<h3>Opening up Government assets - May 2026</h3>
<p>
  The Government made several Government assets publicly available for download on 23 May 2026,
  allowing for greater transparency and open access to information.
</p>
<h3>Implementation of weather updates and search - June 2026</h3>
<p>
  On 2 June 2026, a weather page was added to provide more helpful information to Plushie Kingdom
  residents. Search functionality was also added to enable users to find the information they need
  faster.
</p>
<h3>Improvements to viewing and sharing content - June 2026</h3>
<p>
  On 17 June 2026, a table of contents was added to the start of content pages to make finding
  information easier and faster. A share button was also added for content pages to enable users to
  quickly share relevant information with others.
</p>
<h3>Launch of PIBSS - August 2026</h3>
<p>
  On 6 August 2026, the Plushie Immigration and Biodata Storage Service was introduced to pk-gov.
  This service provides open access to information and statistics on all Plushie Kingdom residents,
  and was pk-gov's largest update ever, containing over 160 commits!
</p>
<h3>Introduction of Timeline - August 2026</h3>
<p>
  On 13 August 2026, Timeline was added to pk-gov as the website's newest service, a public holiday
  tracker that helps to keep plushies' plans on the right track.
</p>
<h3>Revamp of pk-gov layout - September 2026</h3>
<p>
  On 30 September 2026, the aging layout of the pk-gov homepage and footer was revamped to better
  accomodate the many additions to the website since its intiial launch, making it easier for
  plushies to get to the information and services they need. Randomised Bad Guy outfits were also
  added, helping plushies to be more aware of the Bad Guy's appearance.
</p>
<h3>Big year end update - December 2026</h3>
<p>
  On (INSERT DATE HERE), the Ministry of Technology ended 2026 on a high note, delivering many
  updates to pk-gov. Besides cleaning up the codebase, a 404 page was added to guide users who
  navigated to invalid pages. Developer information was also expanded with the introducion of
  pk-dev, providing various technical details about pk-gov. The ability to preview upcoming pk-gov
  updates was also introduced with pk-gov-beta, an alternate website where new features are tested
  before being released on pk-gov.
</p>
